 # Implicit Neural Point Clouds (INPC)
-
+Also called: INPC (Implicit Neural Point Clouds)
 
 ## Overview
-Implicit Neural Point Clouds (INPC) is a point-based neural radiance field method that represents the scene as an implicit point cloud structure using a multi-resolution hash grid and a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) for rendering [S1]. It solves the problem of high-quality novel view synthesis by combining the efficiency of point-based splatting with the flexibility of neural implicit representations [S1]. Unlike its sibling [Neural Point Cloud Renderer](13165-neural-point-cloud-renderer.md), which typically relies on explicit Gaussian or spherical harmonics features attached to points, INPC uses a hash-encoded MLP to predict appearance and opacity, allowing for denser and more continuous feature representation [S1]. It distinguishes itself from other neural implicit methods by utilizing differentiable bilinear splatting for rasterization, enabling efficient gradient-based optimization of both the point positions and the neural network parameters [S1].
+Implicit Neural Point Clouds (INPC) is a point-based neural radiance field method that represents the scene as an implicit point cloud structure using a multi-resolution hash grid and a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) for rendering [S1]. Unlike its sibling [Neural Point Cloud Renderer](13165-neural-point-cloud-renderer.md), which typically relies on explicit Gaussian or spherical harmonics features attached to points, INPC uses a hash-encoded MLP to predict appearance and opacity, allowing for denser and more continuous feature representation [S1]. It distinguishes itself from other neural implicit methods by utilizing differentiable bilinear splatting for rasterization, enabling efficient gradient-based optimization of both the point positions and the neural network parameters [S1].
 
