-*   **Time Complexity:** The rasterization step dominates, involving projection, splatting, sorting, and blending. The use of NVIDIA CUB for sorting and warp-level primitives for blending optimizes this to near-linear time with respect to the number of splats [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the hash grid size ($2^{23}$ entries) and the number of points. The octree structure allows for adaptive resolution, potentially reducing memory usage compared to dense voxel grids [S1].
-*   **Performance:** The method is implemented in CUDA for accelerated rendering times [S1]. The fused blending kernel and efficient sorting contribute to real-time or near-real-time performance depending on resolution and scene complexity [S1].
-*   **Strengths:**
-    *   Flexibility of implicit point cloud structure [S1].
-    *   High-quality reconstruction due to neural feature representation [S1].
-    *   Efficient differentiable rasterization [S1].
-*   **Limitations:**
-    *   Requires careful tuning of hyperparameters (e.g., hash grid size, learning rates) [S1].
-    *   Pre-processing steps (undistortion, normalization) are required for fair comparison with baselines like 3DGS [S1].
